        <div style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border); padding:14px 0;">
            <h3 style="font-size:1rem; margin-bottom:0.4rem;">Why is my security camera feed showing offline or video loss?</h3>
            <p style="color:var(--muted); font-size:0.9rem; line-height:1.7;">Video loss is typically caused by power supply failure, a damaged Ethernet/coaxial cable run, a failed PoE switch port, or an IP address conflict. Our technicians trace the line with digital cable analyzers and diagnostic tools to quickly identify and repair the exact break point.</p>
        </div>

        <div style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border); padding:14px 0;">
            <h3 style="font-size:1rem; margin-bottom:0.4rem;">Can you repair my NVR if it has stopped recording or beeping continuously?</h3>
            <p style="color:var(--muted); font-size:0.9rem; line-height:1.7;">Yes. Continuous beeping and recording stoppage usually indicate a degraded or failed surveillance hard drive, thermal throttling, or corrupted storage partitions. We test drive health on site, replace failed drives with dedicated surveillance-rated storage, and restore scheduled recording.</p>
        </div>

        <div style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border); padding:14px 0;">
